{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"**1) Context7 sources used**\n1. `context7` library resolution: `/websites/platform_openai` (OpenAI Platform) via `resolve-library-id` for “OpenAI”.\n2. `context7` doc fetch attempts for guardrails/prompt injection/fallback topics all returned rate-limit errors, so no authoritative text passages were retrievable in this session.\n\n**2) Findings with severity**\n1. **Medium: capability disclosure can report false negatives during runtime lookup failure**  \n`tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:2514` and `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:2546`  \nIf Firestore lookup fails, `getCompanionRuntimeSelfModel` falls back to `defaultRuntimeSelfModel` (`hasVoiceAccess=false`, `hasVisionAccess=false`, `proactiveEnabled=false`), and the capability overview then states features are “off on your plan.” That is a robustness/truthfulness issue; this should degrade to “unknown” rather than “off”.\n\n2. **Medium: deterministic routing exists, but intent trigger breadth can over-route to capability overview**  \n`tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:354`  \n`directPatterns` includes very broad triggers like `who are you` and `your features`; any such match hard-routes to capability response (`modelUsed: 'capability-router'` at `:3430`). This can suppress normal conversational handling for ambiguous turns and reduces routing precision.\n\n3. **Low-Medium: concise disclosure goal is not met consistently**  \n`tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:473` and `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:495`  \nCapability responses are always long (8 sections + always-on demo prompts for any capability query). This is clear but not concise, and includes promotional comparative language when triggered.\n\n4. **Low: prompt-injection resistance is mostly strong for capability self-description**  \n`tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:428`  \nThe capability overview is template-based and not LLM-generated, which is good. User input only toggles branches (comparison/demo). Residual risk is claim inflation/marketing tone rather than classic prompt injection execution.\n\n5. **Low: guardrail precedence is good but lacks explicit “uncertain intent” path**  \n`tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:3394` then `:3416`  \nOut-of-scope/harmful guardrail executes before capability routing, which is good deterministic ordering. But there is no confidence threshold/ambiguity fallback; single regex hit is enough to route.\n\n**3) Concrete file-level recommendations**\n1. In `defaultRuntimeSelfModel` and `CompanionRuntimeSelfModel`, make `hasVoiceAccess`, `hasVisionAccess`, and `proactiveEnabled` nullable (`boolean | null`) and set fallback values to `null`.  \nFile: `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:102`, `:2514`  \nReason: truthful fallback robustness; unknown should be disclosed as unknown, not off.\n\n2. In `getCompanionRuntimeSelfModel`, return an explicit `dataConfidence`/`source` flag (e.g., `resolved | fallback`) and use it in `buildCapabilityOverviewResponse` to gate certainty language.  \nFile: `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:2546`, `:428`  \nReason: deterministic, auditable disclosure quality.\n\n3. Tighten `detectCapabilityIntent` with stricter patterns and ambiguity handling:\n- Remove or narrow `who are you` catch-all.\n- Require capability nouns/verbs co-occurrence.\n- Add a small score threshold (e.g., 2+ matched cues) before hard route.  \nFile: `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:354`  \nReason: improves deterministic routing precision and reduces false positives.\n\n4. Add a concise mode for capability responses (default short; expand only on explicit ask like “full list”/“details”).  \nFile: `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:428`  \nReason: aligns with concise user-facing capability disclosures.\n\n5. Replace comparative/promotional absolutes with bounded claims and confidence-aware wording (e.g., avoid “more feature-rich than many apps” unless evidence-backed).  \nFile: `tools/girlai2/functions/src/services/llmService.ts:486`  \nReason: safer self-description and lower trust risk.\n\n6. Add targeted unit tests for routing and disclosure behavior:\n- Ambiguous input vs capability route.\n- Runtime lookup failure -> unknown states in response.\n- Harmful+capability mixed input remains blocked.\n- Concise vs expanded disclosure branches.  \nFile target: tests around `detectCapabilityIntent`, `buildCapabilityOverviewResponse`, `generateAIResponse` in the same service module.\n\nI could not retrieve authoritative Context7 guidance text due rate-limiting in this session; findings above are code-grounded and should be treated as a provisional review until Context7 docs can be fetched successfully."}}
